cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "astro-mechinterp: a causal audit of the AION-1 astronomical foundation model"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the manuscript."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Code and per-experiment results for a mechanistic interpretability study of AION-1, a
  multimodal foundation model for astronomy. The study shows that the model defers to
  catalogue-derived metadata over raw pixels, isolates the mechanism as detection gating,
  and quantifies the resulting bias in tomographic mean redshift against the LSST DESC
  requirement.
keywords:
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - foundation models
  - astronomy
  - photometric redshift
  - sparse autoencoders
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "astro-mechinterp contributors"
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: "arXiv:2608.23626"
    description: "arXiv preprint"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "A survey detection channel overrides the pixels in an astronomical foundation model, and biases tomographic mean redshifts"
  year: 2026
  url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.23626"
  authors:
